([Sidenote: Verbal definition of economics]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _Economics, or political economy, may be defined, briefly, as the) Tj T*
(study of men earning a living; or, more fully, as the study of the) Tj T*
(material world and of the activities and mutual relations of men, so far) Tj T*
(as all these are the objective conditions to gratifying desires._ To) Tj T*
(define, means to mark off the limits of a subject, to tell what) Tj T*
(questions are or are not included within it. The ideas of most persons) Tj T*
(on this subject are vague, yet it would be very desirable if the student) Tj T*
(could approach this study with an exact understanding of the nature of) Tj T*
(the questions with which it deals. Until a subject has been studied,) Tj T*
(however, a definition in mere words cannot greatly aid in marking it off) Tj T*
(clearly in our thought. The essential thing for the student is to see) Tj T*
(clearly the central purpose of the study, not to decide at once all of) Tj T*
(the puzzling cases.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Natural sciences deal with material things]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _A definition that suggests clear and familiar thoughts to the) Tj T*
(student seem at first much more difficult to get in any social science) Tj T*
(than in the natural sciences._ These deal with concrete, material things) Tj T*
(which we are accustomed to see, handle, and measure. If a mere child is) Tj T*
(told that botany is a study in which he may learn about flowers, trees,) Tj T*
(and plants, the answer is fairly satisfying, for he at once thinks of) Tj T*
(many things of that kind. When, in like manner zoölogy is defined as the) Tj T*
(study of animals, or geology as the study of rocks and the earth, the) Tj T*
(words call up memories of many familiar objects. Even so difficult and) Tj T*
(foreign-looking a word as ichthyology seems to be made clear by the) Tj T*
(statement that it is the name of the study in which one learns about) Tj T*
(fish. It is true that there may be some misunderstanding as to the way) Tj T*
(in which these subjects are studied, for botany is not in the main to) Tj T*
(teach how to cultivate plants in the garden, nor ichthyology how to) Tj T*
(catch fish or to propagate them in a pond. But the main purpose of these) Tj T*
(studies is clear at the outset from these simple definitions. Indeed, as) Tj T*
(the study is pursued, and knowledge widens to take in the manifold and) Tj T*
(various forms of life, the boundaries of the special sciences become not) Tj T*
(more but less sharp and definite.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Economics studies some social acts and relations]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Political economy, on the other hand, as one of the social sciences,) Tj T*
(which deal with men and their relations in society, seems to be a very) Tj T*
(much more complex thought to get hold of. We are tempted to say that it) Tj T*
(deals with less familiar things; but the truth may be, as a thoughtful) Tj T*
(friend suggests, that the simple social acts and relations are more) Tj T*
(familiar to our thought than are lions, palm-trees, or even horses.) Tj T*
(Every hour in the streets or stores, one may witness thousands of acts,) Tj T*
(such as bargains, labor, payments, that are the subject-matter of) Tj T*
(economic science. Their very familiarity may cause men to overlook their) Tj T*
(deeper meaning.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
