() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Economic study needed in a democracy]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _But, in the main, the study of political economy is a social study) Tj T*
(for social ends and not a selfish study for individual advantage._ The) Tj T*
(name political economy was first suggested in France when the government) Tj T*
(was monarchical and despotic in the extreme. As domestic economy) Tj T*
(indicates a set of rules or principles to guide wisely the action of) Tj T*
(the housekeeper or the owner of an estate, so political economy was) Tj T*
(first thought of as a set of rules or principles to guide the king and) Tj T*
(his counselors in the control of the state. The term has continued to) Tj T*
(bear something of that suggestion in it, though of late the term) Tj T*
("economics," as being broader and less likely to be confused with) Tj T*
(politics, has very generally come into use. But in the degree in which) Tj T*
(unlimited monarchy has given way to the rule of the people, the) Tj T*
(conception of political economy has been modified. In a democracy there) Tj T*
(is need for a general diffusion of knowledge. The power now rests not) Tj T*
(with the king and a few counselors, but in the last resort with the) Tj T*
(people, and therefore the people must be acquainted with the experience) Tj T*
(of the past, must have all possible systematic knowledge to enlighten) Tj T*
(public policy and to guide legislation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Is of growing interest and influence]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Moreover, with the growth of the modern state, with the interest) Tj T*
(increasing importance of business, and of industrial and commercial) Tj T*
(interests, as compared with changes of dynasty or the personal rivalries) Tj T*
(of rulers, economic questions have grown in relative importance. In our) Tj T*
(own country, particularly since the subjects of slavery and of States') Tj T*
(rights ceased to absorb the attention of our people, economic questions) Tj T*
(have pushed rapidly into the foreground. Indeed, it has of late been) Tj T*
(more clearly seen that many of the older political questions, such as) Tj T*
(the American Revolution and slavery, formerly discussed almost entirely) Tj T*
(in their political and constitutional aspects, were at bottom questions) Tj T*
(of economic rivalry and of economic welfare. The remarkable increase in) Tj T*
(the attention given to this study in colleges and universities in the) Tj T*
(last twenty years is but the index of the greatly increased interest and) Tj T*
(attention felt in it by citizens generally.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
