BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(4. _In human society, wants develop and transform the world._ In the) Tj T*
(rudest societies of which there is any record, savages are found with) Tj T*
(wants developed in a great number of directions beyond the wants of any) Tj T*
(animals. Man is not a passive victim of circumstances; his wants are not) Tj T*
(determined solely by his environment; his desires soar beyond the things) Tj T*
(about him. As men become more the masters of circumstances, their) Tj T*
(desires anticipate mere physical wants; they seek a more varied food of) Tj T*
(finer flavor and more delicately prepared. Dress is not limited by) Tj T*
(physical comfort, for one of the earliest of the esthetic wants to) Tj T*
(develop is the love of personal ornament. The rude hut or communal lodge) Tj T*
