() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Recognition of diminishing returns to land]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _The law of "diminishing returns" was first recognized and expressed) Tj T*
(with reference to the use of land in agriculture._ There are several) Tj T*
(evident reasons why this occurred. It is obvious to every farmer and) Tj T*
(gardener that he cannot indefinitely increase his crop, that two men) Tj T*
(cannot always produce twice as much as one man, and that in general the) Tj T*
(product does not always vary in proportion to the labor and materials) Tj T*
(applied. Moreover, the food supply is a fundamental factor in industry) Tj T*
(and in the welfare of states. The limit to the supply of food on a given) Tj T*
(area, cultivated by a given method, early appeared and became a serious) Tj T*
(practical problem.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The circumstances in Europe in the eighteenth century drew attention to) Tj T*
(the subject. Population was increasing, and the pressure for food was) Tj T*
(strong. While all the forms of industry most common in cities were) Tj T*
(increasing, and the wealth of the cities was growing, poverty was) Tj T*
(increasing among the peasantry. Especially was this true in England) Tj T*
(during the Napoleonic wars, 1793-1815, owing to exceptional conditions.) Tj T*
(The food-supply from abroad was cut off, and when the English farmers,) Tj T*
(tempted by the high prices, took poorer land into cultivation, and) Tj T*
(sought to get larger crops from their older fields, a great) Tj T*
(object-lesson was presented on the principle of diminishing returns in) Tj T*
(agriculture.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: This confused with historical diminishing returns]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
