(1. _A large part of industry is now conducted without regard to the) Tj T*
(preservation of the source of income._ A striking example of this is the) Tj T*
(use, or rather the destruction, of the American forests. In the last) Tj T*
(century the demand for lumber grew rapidly both on account of domestic) Tj T*
(needs and of the needs of the older countries. Great quantities of wood) Tj T*
(have been used and still greater quantities wasted, trees being girdled,) Tj T*
(the ground burned over, the timber destroyed in any way that would clear) Tj T*
(the soil--timber which to-day would be of far more value than is the) Tj T*
(cleared land on which it stood. Considering present needs and) Tj T*
(conditions, the labor seems to have been worse than wasted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
