(their rents._ Farm land of the poorest kind often is found to contain) Tj T*
(valuable mineral deposits. Such a lucky find has lifted the mortgage) Tj T*
(from a farm in eastern Pennsylvania, from which, in two or three years,) Tj T*
(has been taken feldspar exceeding in value the agricultural products of) Tj T*
(the same land in the last fifty years. The discovery of building stone,) Tj T*
(coal, natural gas, or oil land may make the annual rent \(or royalty\) of) Tj T*
(land tenfold its former total value. Fitness to produce nettles is not) Tj T*
(ordinarily a virtue in land, but the discovery that certain fields) Tj T*
(produce a superior quality of the nettle used for heckling cloth, causes) Tj T*
