() Tj T*
(1. _In the case of consumption goods, present marginal uses are often) Tj T*
(less than future uses as judged at the present._ The proposition that) Tj T*
(future goods sometimes have a greater instead of a less value than) Tj T*
(present goods may at first seem to deny the general fact of economic) Tj T*
(interest, which is a premium on present over future goods. The) Tj T*
(contradiction is only apparent, however, and the proposition is merely a) Tj T*
(proper interpretation of the theory of interest. The assertion that) Tj T*
(present goods have greater value than future goods, as we have accepted) Tj T*
(it, requires two explanations. First, it means that this difference) Tj T*
(exists when the two are judged and compared _at the present moment_. The) Tj T*
(future use when it matures may be much greater than the present use;) Tj T*
(indeed, the very existence of interest depends upon this surplus of) Tj T*
(value arising by the lapse of time in the future use. Secondly, the) Tj T*
(proposition does not mean that every concrete good, or every use of the) Tj T*
(goods, is worth more in the present than in the future; it means merely) Tj T*
(that the demand for present goods preponderates so that a market rate in) Tj T*
(favor of present possession prevails. In a great many cases a particular) Tj T*
(good may have a greater value to be kept for the future than to be used) Tj T*
(at present, in which case it is kept, or it is exchanged for something) Tj T*
(else having a higher value in the present. But this preference of the) Tj T*
(future over the present cannot pass a moderate limit without condemning) Tj T*
(the person to present misery, and at length to death. On the other hand) Tj T*
(the excessive preference of present over future would lead to the using) Tj T*
(up and wearing out of wealth, to the present enjoyment of every possible) Tj T*
(resource, on the penalty of future misery. Evidently somewhere between) Tj T*
(these two extremes there must be, in each economy, a ratio of exchange) Tj T*
(between present and future, which in fact is the interest rate. This) Tj T*
(rate applied to utilities traces through each good a line analagous to) Tj T*
(the isothermal line on the map, marking off a zone of utilities for the) Tj T*
(present and other zones for each period of the future. There is thus a) Tj T*
(close relation between saving and the rate of time-discount.) Tj T*
