() Tj T*
(1. _Political security and domestic order are essential to the) Tj T*
(development of saving._ As saving results from a comparison of the) Tj T*
(future with the present, any lack of certainty regarding the future) Tj T*
(decreases the appeal it makes. Men employ roughly the theory of) Tj T*
(probabilities in this matter, and count a utility only half as much) Tj T*
(when there is but one chance in two of enjoying it. In countries where) Tj T*
(there are constant revolutions and border wars, as in Africa and South) Tj T*
(America, and in lands where brigandage is common, as in Italy,) Tj T*
(Macedonia, and Bulgaria, the motive for saving is cut in two. Oppressive) Tj T*
(and irregular taxation kills the motives of providence, and decreases) Tj T*
(the appeal made by the future. While the miserable subjects of the state) Tj T*
(live from hand to mouth, the very sources of the public revenue) Tj T*
(disappear. Improvidence grows upon such a people into a prevailing) Tj T*
(national custom; ambition is wanting; industry is the sport of chance;) Tj T*
(economic order and economic prosperity are impossible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
