() Tj T*
(4. _Variations in the rate of discount of the future react upon the) Tj T*
(spirit of saving in various ways._ This very general proposition) Tj T*
(requires more detailed discussion. In general, a high rate of interest) Tj T*
(gives a large motive to save, for as the discount on the future is) Tj T*
(large, so is the reward for waiting. But this favoring motive may be) Tj T*
(offset by other unfavorable conditions, and is, in fact, wherever the) Tj T*
(high rate continues. In countries backward economically, where war,) Tj T*
(brigandage, and political oppression prevail, the rate of interest is) Tj T*
(frequently ten and twelve per cent. on the best secured loans. A high) Tj T*
(interest rate does not of itself insure a high degree of cumulative) Tj T*
(abstinence; it is only one of several factors. But in a new and favored) Tj T*
(country like America, a high rate of interest is a strong stimulus to) Tj T*
(saving. Again, interest may fall while saving continues at the same or a) Tj T*
(greater pace. Ordinarily a fall from six per cent. to five, giving men) Tj T*
(a smaller motive for abstinence, would be expected to cause less saving,) Tj T*
(yet this is not always the case. Custom and example help to fix a habit) Tj T*
(of saving in individuals and cause them to continue saving at a lower) Tj T*
(rate of interest. With the growth of wealth, the prevailing ideas as to) Tj T*
(the amount needed for a competence change, impelling to greater saving.) Tj T*
(The tendency, however, of a fall in the rate of interest is to weaken,) Tj T*
(and that of a rise of the rate, other things being equal, is to) Tj T*
(strengthen the motive to save. But the influence of the interest rate on) Tj T*
(saving is relative to the character of men.) Tj T*
