(4. _A fall in the rate of interest normally accompanies an increase in) Tj T*
(the mass, efficiency, and valuation of durable economic agents._ A lower) Tj T*
(rate of interest means a higher capitalization of all incomes. It is not) Tj T*
(that either can be called the cause of the other; rather both are) Tj T*
(aspects of the same thing, the interest rate merely registering the) Tj T*
(change in capitalization. If the rate of interest has been five per) Tj T*
(cent., an income of $100 has been capitalized at $2000. When the rate) Tj T*
(falls to four per cent. the income is recapitalized at $2500. All along) Tj T*
(the line of investment there is an increase in the value of the durable) Tj T*
(economic agents.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: And more complex industrial processes]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
