(operation]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another phase of the change is the greater complexity of the processes) Tj T*
(of industry. Production becomes technically more complex when interest) Tj T*
(falls. Rental, product, and present goods, bear a smaller ratio to the) Tj T*
(value of capital, and therefore it becomes advantageous to apply newly) Tj T*
(formed capital to uses which before did not justify the investment.) Tj T*
(Where formerly the utility of a second tool did not justify its making,) Tj T*
(now it can be made to earn the smaller rental needed to balance its) Tj T*
(capital value. One form, therefore, which the change takes, is a) Tj T*
(multiplication of the tools already used. Things are placed wherever) Tj T*
(most convenient. Another form this change takes is the putting of new) Tj T*
(links into the chain of technical production. Cost of operation) Tj T*
(constantly is compared with fixed charges, the interest with the capital) Tj T*
(investment. Expensive improvements on railroads, the straightening of) Tj T*
(curves, the tunneling of mountains, the reducing of grades, the) Tj T*
(replacement of lighter by heavier rails, have been made possible by a) Tj T*
(fall in the rate of interest. A fall in the rate of interest disturbs) Tj T*
(the equilibrium that has been arrived at, between the cost of operation,) Tj T*
(the amount paid for wages, coal, etc., and the income on permanent) Tj T*
(investment. If the rate of interest has been five per cent. and falls) Tj T*
(to four per cent. many permanent improvements before unwise become) Tj T*
(economical. One thousand dollars paid annually in wages then balanced an) Tj T*
(interest charge on a capital investment of $20,000; now it balances the) Tj T*
(interest charge on $25,000. It becomes a paying thing for the railroad) Tj T*
(to abandon or throw aside an enormous capital represented by the old,) Tj T*
(less perfect roadbed, and build a new one alongside of it. The changes) Tj T*
(of this kind one sees in traveling on the great and progressive) Tj T*
(railroads, reflect in part the growth of traffic, but in part also a) Tj T*
(change of the interest rate, making it a net saving to increase the) Tj T*
(capital investment in order to reduce the cost of operation per unit of) Tj T*
(traffic.) Tj T*
