([Sidenote: The gloomy view as to the wage system was mistaken]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Seventy-five years ago it was thought that, with the increase of) Tj T*
(machinery, of factories, of the concentrated control of wealth, and) Tj T*
(especially with the wage system, there must go a steady depression in) Tj T*
(the welfare of the workingman. This idea was connected with the iron law) Tj T*
(of wages. It was believed by some that, whatever the causes of advancing) Tj T*
(social income might be, the wage system would rob the wage-earners of) Tj T*
(all share in progress. In view of the facts, if it cannot now be) Tj T*
(asserted positively that the wage system is the cause of all the gain,) Tj T*
(it can be asserted negatively that it is not inconsistent with great) Tj T*
(progress on the part of the laboring classes. It might be possible to go) Tj T*
(further and to maintain that the organization of industry, under the) Tj T*
(wage system and competitive conditions, by its encouragement of) Tj T*
(enterprise, energy, and economy, has been an indispensable condition in) Tj T*
(the industrial progress which has in turn made possible the rising wages) Tj T*
(of labor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
