(§ I. EXTENT OF THE USE OF MACHINERY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Tools, machines, and power]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _A machine is a mechanical device by which power is applied in an) Tj T*
(automatically repeated manner, to change the place or form of things._) Tj T*
(It is not easy, perhaps not important, to distinguish the machine from) Tj T*
(the tool in every case. Tools are portions of matter, such as bone,) Tj T*
(wood, iron, which man guides and directs in applying his energy to) Tj T*
(things. A machine may be used by the foot, but the hand is the great) Tj T*
(tool-using member. In many cases there is a clearly marked distinction) Tj T*
(between tool and machine. A simple, single piece that can be taken into) Tj T*
(the hand, as a spade, a hammer, a knife, is a tool; a combination of) Tj T*
(wheels, levers, pulleys, etc., is a machine. The simplest machine is but) Tj T*
(a slight adaptation of the tool, by which power may be applied in an) Tj T*
(automatically repeated manner. The drag develops into the cart, a simple) Tj T*
(machine. The spinning-stick, a tool used in ancient times, developed) Tj T*
(into the Saxon spinning-wheel of the sixteenth century, the form used) Tj T*
(when America was colonized. The use of power derived from nature, as) Tj T*
(that of wind and water and steam, while not the essential mark of) Tj T*
(machines, is the most characteristic feature of their modern) Tj T*
(development. Hand-machines, such as the hand-press and the type-writer,) Tj T*
(have had important industrial results, but it is the use of power) Tj T*
(leading to the concentration of industry and the ownership of machinery) Tj T*
(by the employers that has the greatest significance in the modern) Tj T*
(economic problem.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Machinery brought in an industrial revolution]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _Machinery of many sorts has long been used, but the "age of) Tj T*
(machinery" begins with the eighteenth century._ Inventions, new) Tj T*
(machines, and new processes, though not frequent, were not unknown in) Tj T*
(the Middle Ages; but no one class of machines took possession of a whole) Tj T*
(field of industry and gave rise to a great economic problem by the) Tj T*
(displacing of labor. The great industrial changes in the Middle Ages) Tj T*
(generally grew out of political changes, or of changes of routes of) Tj T*
(trade whereby large industries were disturbed, or of changes in the use) Tj T*
(of land through new methods and the bringing into use of land in other) Tj T*
(places. The industrial changes in England at the end of the eighteenth) Tj T*
(century on the contrary were due mainly to great mechanical inventions.) Tj T*
(The development of the textile machines for cotton and wool spinning and) Tj T*
(weaving mark the beginning of the movement. Here for the first time were) Tj T*
(inventions in such numbers, of such a nature, and under such conditions,) Tj T*
