([Sidenote: Acquisition vs. social production]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. _Individual acquisition may be contrasted with social production in) Tj T*
(cases where the individual increases his wealth at the expense of) Tj T*
(others, without adding to value._ Most economic efforts increase the) Tj T*
(income of the individual and the income of society at the same time. The) Tj T*
(fruits of the field and the uses of machines are net additions to) Tj T*
(current income; they are not merely subtracted from the income of one) Tj T*
(and added to that of another. The increase of products by labor may) Tj T*
(depress somewhat the exchange value of competing labor, but the general) Tj T*
(welfare is furthered by the greater abundance. With very slight) Tj T*
(qualification it is true that in these cases the good of each is the) Tj T*
(good of all. But in some forms of human effort, social and individual) Tj T*
(interests clash. When two men bet, one gains and the other loses. The) Tj T*
(gambler's gain is a loss not only directly to his beaten opponent but) Tj T*
(indirectly to society. Certain forms of speculation approach dangerously) Tj T*
(near to the appropriation of the goods of others, and others become) Tj T*
(outright stealing, or cheating so nearly like stealing that it would be) Tj T*
(treated as a crime if discovered. But many a man prowls along the) Tj T*
(border-line of crime all his life and succeeds in making large gains) Tj T*
(without falling into the clutches of the law. Cheating that can be) Tj T*
(detected, and outright stealing, are prohibited by the law not because) Tj T*
(the burglar is an idler; he loses sleep; he has his trials too. The) Tj T*
(pursuit of burglary requires courage, effort, and ingenuity, but society) Tj T*
(does not reward these as virtues nor recognize as production the) Tj T*
(transfer of wealth from the bank-vault to the pocket of the burglar. It) Tj T*
(is the aim of social institutions to harmonize individual and social) Tj T*
(interests in the pursuit of wealth, to force men into lines of action) Tj T*
(where individual acquisition adds to the sum of social utilities. But) Tj T*
(there are many marginal cases where human justice discriminates only in) Tj T*
(a bungling way, and many controverted questions arise at the) Tj T*
(meeting-point of ethics, economics, and law.) Tj T*
