(This is one of the greatest sources of America's superiority to-day. It) Tj T*
(has been strikingly said that it is now no longer "young America and old) Tj T*
(Europe," but "old America and young Europe." America is older in) Tj T*
(industrial experience; Europe, with undeveloped resources, awaits the) Tj T*
(touch of American methods and machinery. There are dynamic forces in) Tj T*
(American society not present in equal degree in any other. It is) Tj T*
(therefore not alone the great resources of coal and iron,--equal) Tj T*
(resources may be found in unexplored parts of the world,--it is the) Tj T*
(dynamic social forces, invention, enterprise, and organization, which) Tj T*
