(4. _A high efficiency of industry is dependent on many social causes) Tj T*
(making possible a great specialization._ It was said in another) Tj T*
(connection that division of labor is dependent upon the size of the) Tj T*
(market. With a large population massed at one spot, so that the demand) Tj T*
(for even the less important products is large, there may be a high) Tj T*
(specialization of industry. An increase of transportation, such as) Tj T*
(railways and telegraphs, is equivalent for many economic purposes to) Tj T*
(growth of population on one spot. In colonial days it took ten days to) Tj T*
(go from Boston to Philadelphia, and two weeks to go to Washington. San) Tj T*
(Francisco is now for many economic purposes but one fourth as far from) Tj T*
(Boston as Washington was at that time. California and the eastern states) Tj T*
(are distant only thirty minutes by telegraph and three days and a) Tj T*
(fraction by railroad, and are thus in many respects in the same market.) Tj T*
(The great development during the past century in the means of) Tj T*
(communication and of carriage has made possible, as never before, the) Tj T*
(massing of population to secure the advantages of division of labor in) Tj T*
(most lines, without meeting the hitherto insurmountable difficulty in) Tj T*
(the securing of food for such large numbers in a limited space. The) Tj T*
(population draws its food from the whole vast area; whereas it is massed) Tj T*
(at the points more favorable for other products and can make use of the) Tj T*
(most highly specialized machinery. These several conditions thus have) Tj T*
(favored the growth of large industry under a single control and) Tj T*
(direction, on a scale never before approached. These changes have) Tj T*
(brought in their train social problems connected with the concentration) Tj T*
(of economic power. It remains to be seen whether the unquestioned) Tj T*
(economies of this new organization can be retained and improved while it) Tj T*
(is divested of its evils.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
