([Sidenote: Definition of monopoly]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Monopoly limits supply]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. _Monopoly is such a degree of control over the supply of goods in a) Tj T*
(given market that a net gain will result to the seller if a portion is) Tj T*
(withheld._ Every producer has control over some agents and some portion) Tj T*
(of the supply of products; but ordinarily the portion controlled by any) Tj T*
(one is so small that withholding it entirely from sale would not cause) Tj T*
(the market price to rise in any appreciable degree. The producer in such) Tj T*
(a case regulates his action as if the market price were fixed beyond his) Tj T*
(control, and he uses his productive agents fully up to the point where) Tj T*
(costs equal price on the marginal unit of product. A skilled worker) Tj T*
(getting five dollars a day loses that sum every day he is idle. A) Tj T*
(landowner whose land can command a competitive rent of ten dollars an) Tj T*
(acre must take that sum or less, or nothing; he cannot get more. How can) Tj T*
(a net gain ever result from a smaller sale? As a reduction of supply) Tj T*
(results in a higher price, it is possible, as is seen in the paradox of) Tj T*
(value, for a situation to arise in the case of some goods, where a) Tj T*
(smaller number of units yield a larger sum in the market than a larger) Tj T*
(number of units. But the seller's interest lies not in the increase of) Tj T*
(total sales, but in that of net gains. Net gains, being the product of) Tj T*
(the number of units sold multiplied by the gain on each unit, increase) Tj T*
(at a much faster rate than do total sales. The existence of monopoly) Tj T*
(power in any degree depends therefore on several factors: the effect of) Tj T*
(contraction of supply in raising prices, the effect on costs, the number) Tj T*
(of units remaining in the ownership of the one contracting supply, and) Tj T*
(the possibility of preventing others from increasing supply later to) Tj T*
(profit by the higher prices.) Tj T*
