(§ II. KINDS OF MONOPOLY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: The sources of monopoly power]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Political monopoly]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _Monopoly gets its power from political, economic, and commercial) Tj T*
(sources._ A political monopoly derives its power of control from a) Tj T*
(special grant from the government, forbidding others to engage in that) Tj T*
(business. The typical political monopoly is that conferred by a crown) Tj T*
(patent bestowing the exclusive right to carry on a certain business. A) Tj T*
(second kind is that conferred by a patent for invention, or the) Tj T*
(copyright on books, the object of which is to stimulate invention,) Tj T*
(research, and writing by giving the full control and protection of the) Tj T*
(government to the inventor and writer or their assignees. In this case) Tj T*
(the privilege is socially earned by the monopolist; it is not gotten for) Tj T*
(nothing. Moreover, the patent is limited in time, expires and becomes a) Tj T*
(social possession. A third kind is a government monopoly for purposes) Tj T*
(of revenue. In France, the government controls the tobacco trade, and) Tj T*
(the high price charged for tobacco makes the monopoly yield a large) Tj T*
(income. A fourth kind are public franchises for public service, as) Tj T*
(street-railways, lights, gas, waterworks, etc. These are granted to) Tj T*
(private capitalists to induce them to invest capital in something which) Tj T*
(has public utility.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Economic monopoly]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Economic monopoly arises when the ownership of scarce natural agents, as) Tj T*
(mines, land, water-power, comes under the control of one man or one) Tj T*
(group of men who agree on a price. Economic monopoly is a result of) Tj T*
(private property that is undesigned by the government or by society. It) Tj T*
(is exceptional, considering the whole range of private property, but it) Tj T*
(is important. The oil-wells embracing the main sources of the world's) Tj T*
(supply have come under one control. One corporation may control so many) Tj T*
(of the richest iron-mines of the country as to be able to fix a price) Tj T*
(different from that which would result under competition. Coal-mines,) Tj T*
(especially those of some peculiar and limited kind, such as anthracite,) Tj T*
(appear to become easily an object of monopolization. Economic monopoly) Tj T*
(merges into political monopolies, such as patents and franchises.) Tj T*
(Private property is a political institution designed to further social) Tj T*
(welfare, and only rarely is any particular property a monopoly. Private) Tj T*
(control of great natural resources doubtless would have been prohibited) Tj T*
(had it been foreseen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Commercial monopoly]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Commercial monopoly, variously called contractual, organized, or) Tj T*
(capitalistic monopoly, arises where men unite their wealth to control a) Tj T*
(market, to overpower or intimidate opposition, and to keep out or limit) Tj T*
(competition by the mere magnitude of their wealth. These various kinds) Tj T*
(so merge into each other that they cannot always be distinguished in) Tj T*
(practice. A patent may help a capitalistic monopoly in getting control) Tj T*
