(confidence imposed in a trustee. The method that was adopted by the) Tj T*
(early combinations was the trust method, that is, they made use of this) Tj T*
(legal device: the stock of the separate companies was put into the hands) Tj T*
(of a board of trustees to whom was thus given the right to control. As) Tj T*
(it has been found possible to accomplish the same end without the use of) Tj T*
(this legal method, the popular meaning of the word trust, as applied to) Tj T*
(a monopoly, no longer agrees with the legal meaning. The word trust is) Tj T*
(popularly used of any large industry, though usually there is connected) Tj T*
(with it the idea of some evil power to raise prices to the consumers. A) Tj T*
(large number of the corporations called trusts have, however, little) Tj T*
