([Sidenote: Unavoidable chances]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _Many forms of chance are inseparable from the individual) Tj T*
(enterprise._ There are what may be called natural chances chances,) Tj T*
(arising from the uncertainties of the seasons, from rainfall, heat,) Tj T*
(hail, storm, flood, lightning, land-slides. Such chances must be taken) Tj T*
(both by the small enterpriser and by the large. In an earlier condition) Tj T*
(of society natural chance almost dominated industry, and it still) Tj T*
(remains and must always remain an important factor to deal with. There) Tj T*
(are political chances, as war and riot; as legislation on money,) Tj T*
