() Tj T*
(The period from 1897 to 1903 has been marked by great prosperity and by) Tj T*
(rising prices. The over-hasty prophecies of collapse in the last two) Tj T*
(years have thus far been falsified,[3] but there is now a general) Tj T*
(feeling of distrust in investing circles. Already there has been a) Tj T*
(reduction of dividends in leading industries, and here and there a fall) Tj T*
(in the value of stocks. High prices have greatly checked building. The) Tj T*
(great credit advances made on "industrials," the stocks of manufacturing) Tj T*
(corporations, are one of the main sources of danger. Caution, however,) Tj T*
(has been learned by experience; the banking interests are more closely) Tj T*
(coördinated and give better mutual support than in the past, and a) Tj T*
