() Tj T*
(§ III. VARIOUS EXPLANATIONS OF CRISES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Glut theories of crises]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _Over-production and under-consumption theories are those most widely) Tj T*
(held._ In the first annual report of the United States Commissioner of) Tj T*
(Labor \(1886\) is given a long list of theories, more or less wild, that) Tj T*
(have been advanced in explanation of crises. It is simply a catalogue,) Tj T*
(not a logical grouping. Most of the views can be classed as) Tj T*
(under-consumption or over-production theories, which are but two aspects) Tj T*
(of the same idea. One view is that too many things are produced, another) Tj T*
(that too few are consumed. The over-production theorist, seeing that) Tj T*
(warehouses are filled with goods that cannot be disposed of for what) Tj T*
(they cost, that factories are shut down and men are out of employment) Tj T*
(for lack of demand, declares that productive power has grown too great.) Tj T*
(The under-consumption theorist, seeing the same facts, says that the) Tj T*
(trouble is lack of purchasing power. He admits that there are people who) Tj T*
(would like to buy these things, but he asserts that such people lack) Tj T*
(money because production grows faster than wages, wages being fixed, as) Tj T*
(he believes, by the minimum of subsistence--a theory akin to the iron) Tj T*
(law of wages. In both over-production and under-consumption theories the) Tj T*
(inequality of demand and supply is looked upon as a general one. There) Tj T*
(is supposed to be not merely an unequal and mistaken distribution of) Tj T*
(production, but a general excess of productive power.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Defects of glut theories]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The wide vogue held by these views would justify a fuller discussion and) Tj T*
(disproof of them here, did space permit. It must suffice to indicate) Tj T*
(merely that they have the same taint of illogicalness as the "fallacy of) Tj T*
(waste," the "fallacy of saving" and, still closer likeness, the "fallacy) Tj T*
(of luxury." They overlook the fact that an income, either of money or of) Tj T*
(other goods, coming even to the wealthiest, will be used in some way. It) Tj T*
(may be used either for immediate consumption or for further indirect use) Tj T*
(in durable form. Through miscalculation there may be, at a given moment,) Tj T*
(too many consumption goods of a particular kind, but the durable) Tj T*
(applications can find no limit until the inconceivable day when the) Tj T*
(material world is no longer capable of improvement. At the time of a) Tj T*
(crisis, there is unquestionably a bad apportionment of productive) Tj T*
(agents, and a still worse adjustment of their valuations, but these in) Tj T*
(no wise negative the basic economic fact of the scarcity of wealth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Money theories of crises]) Tj T*
