(rush toward this or that investment, throwing capitalization in some) Tj T*
(industries far out of equilibrium with that in others.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The use of credit enhances the rhythm of price. A large part of business) Tj T*
(is done practically on margins. If the value of a thing fully paid for) Tj T*
(falls in the hands of the owner, he alone loses; but if the value of a) Tj T*
(thing only partly paid for falls so much that the owner is forced to) Tj T*
(default in his payment, the loss may be transmitted along the line of) Tj T*
(credit to every one in the series of transactions. A credit system,) Tj T*
(highly developed, is a house of cards at a time of financial stress.) Tj T*
(There is an element of credit in all modern business. Enterprisers enter) Tj T*
(into strenuous rivalry to secure the profits of a rise, ever hoping to) Tj T*
(get out whole before the crisis comes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Psychological nature and objective conditions of crises]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fundamental cause of crises thus is seen to be psychological; it is) Tj T*
(the rhythmic miscalculation of rents and of capital value, occurring to) Tj T*
(some degree throughout industry, but particularly in certain lines. But) Tj T*
(this subjective cause in men is given full opportunity for action only) Tj T*
(when certain favoring objective conditions are present. Most noteworthy) Tj T*
(of these besides the credit system is a dynamic condition of industry.) Tj T*
(The past century has opened up new fields for investment on an) Tj T*
(unexampled scale. Investment has advanced both intensively and) Tj T*
(extensively in a series of great waves. New machinery and processes have) Tj T*
(given undreamed of opportunities for enterprise in the older countries,) Tj T*
(and the physical frontier of investment has moved outward with the march) Tj T*
(of millions of immigrants to people the fertile wilderness. Such factors) Tj T*
(disturb the equilibrium of prices both in time and space, give a) Tj T*
(powerful impulse toward higher values in the older lands, and stimulate) Tj T*
(the hopes of all investors. When the balance between the capitalizations) Tj T*
(of various industries and between the rents of the various periods) Tj T*
(proves to be false, the inevitable readjustment causes suffering and) Tj T*
(loss to many, but particularly in the inflated industries. But, because) Tj T*
(of the mutual relations of men in business, few even of those who have) Tj T*
(kept freest from speculation can quite escape the evils.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Widespread effects on incomes]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. _Crises must be discussed in connection with other subjects than) Tj T*
(profits._ In the text-books the subject of the crisis is variously) Tj T*
(classified. It may well be discussed with money, credit, and banking. It) Tj T*
(has its bearings on wages, justice in distribution, the theory of) Tj T*
(interest, and the consumption of wealth. But the reasons for taking it) Tj T*
