(length to respond to natural pleasures. When the senses are robbed of) Tj T*
(their fineness, youth grows blasé, mature manhood is ennuied, life is) Tj T*
(empty. The praise of "the simple life" has lately been heard in a) Tj T*
(quarter whence such counsel does not usually come. In gay Paris, a wise) Tj T*
(pastor has made one of the most beautiful and rational pleas for plain) Tj T*
(and sincere living that society has heard since the time of the stoic) Tj T*
(philosophers. The word is needed. With the growth of incomes grows the) Tj T*
(strain to reach the self-imposed standards of frivolity. Insanity and) Tj T*
(suicide are on the increase. The stress of modern life makes men yearn) Tj T*
(for the simpler joys. Happiness dwells not outside of men; they must) Tj T*
(seek it within.) Tj T*
