(a social process. The different agents are complementary goods, each) Tj T*
(necessary to the best use of the various other agents. The value of seed) Tj T*
(is not to be found apart from the use of the ground; or the value of the) Tj T*
(leather apart from the shoemaker or the thread he uses. When these) Tj T*
(things are brought together in society their value is found by the) Tj T*
(comparison and measurement of marginal utilities. Economic forces, like) Tj T*
(other classes of forces, act and react upon each other. Two bodies) Tj T*
(attract each other in space; two chemicals uniting are both transformed) Tj T*
(into a substance differing from either. The economic result of materials) Tj T*
(and men coöperating is something differing from either factor, yet) Tj T*
(dependent on both.) Tj T*
