(sustained.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Good social effects of self-interest]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Through self-interest the working force is distributed over the field of) Tj T*
(industry wherever it is most needed. The remarkable adjustment of) Tj T*
(industry to the needs of each neighborhood is brought about by) Tj T*
(individual motives, not by centralized authority. It is not mere chance) Tj T*
(that produces this harmony. Wherever consumers settle, stores are) Tj T*
(started and factories are built. Wherever work is to be done, men come) Tj T*
(in about the right number to do it. Skill is adjusted to needs by the) Tj T*
(delicate measurement of the market rate of wages. Competition gives a) Tj T*
(definite rule of price--certainly the only definite impersonal rule;) Tj T*
(some say the only just rule. The competitive price must be appealed to) Tj T*
(even in arbitration. It is the standard to which things tend constantly) Tj T*
(to adjust themselves in an open market.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Conflicting interests in the business world]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. _Experience shows that the economic interests of men are only partly,) Tj T*
(not wholly, in harmony._ That there is a great measure of truth in the) Tj T*
(statements just made, all must admit; but their application is limited.) Tj T*
(They are partial truths, never to be ignored, but quite false if taken,) Tj T*
(without modification, as practical rules of conduct. There are three) Tj T*
(species of competition in every market: that between sellers, that) Tj T*
(between buyers, and that between sellers on the one hand and buyers on) Tj T*
(the other. It is to the interest of the buyers that the sellers shall be) Tj T*
(numerous, eager, and freely competing. It is to the interest of the) Tj T*
(seller that supply shall be small, that sellers shall be united, and) Tj T*
(that buyers shall compete sharply. If at any point free competition is) Tj T*
(hindered, even the disciple of economic harmony must expect a discordant) Tj T*
(result. But in reality competition is rarely quite complete on both) Tj T*
(sides, and when it is not, the weak suffer. Men do not start with fair) Tj T*
(and equal opportunities. All that they may be entitled to under) Tj T*
(competition may be so little that social sympathy seeks to better the) Tj T*
(result; hence poor relief, public and private. Society as a whole has an) Tj T*
(interest in the outcome of the individual's economic struggle. It cannot) Tj T*
(see men starving or driven into crime. But the argument need not be) Tj T*
(confined to such crude and extreme cases, for wherever economic) Tj T*
(interests are not in harmony and it is possible to further the social) Tj T*
(welfare, will not society be justified in acting?) Tj T*
