([Sidenote: Imperfections of economic freedom]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _Undoubted evils result from some forms of competition under the) Tj T*
(conditions actually existing._ Complete freedom must remain a somewhat) Tj T*
(abstract ideal, and actual conditions must be recognized. Entire freedom) Tj T*
(of choice means freedom to make mistakes, a privilege whose enjoyment) Tj T*
(society cannot always permit. The child should be raised to good) Tj T*
(citizenship, and entire freedom of choice makes that impossible or) Tj T*
(improbable. The freedom of choice of the insane, the feeble-minded, and) Tj T*
(the criminal, cannot be recognized. Even where competition is the ideal) Tj T*
(of sound adult humanity, it is not to be too suddenly or extremely) Tj T*
(applied. The inequality of faculties, the prevailing dishonesty, the) Tj T*
(mass of inherited abuses, cannot be either ignored or at once ended. The) Tj T*
(immigrant from Europe, plunged into the trying conditions of city life,) Tj T*
(suffers in health and in morals, and often becomes a burden upon) Tj T*
(society. One of many competitors may drive competition to an evil) Tj T*
(extreme. The "problem of the twentieth man" is presented when nineteen) Tj T*
(men desire to limit competition in ways not socially harmful, as by) Tj T*
(closing shops on Sunday or in the evening, and the one man refuses. The) Tj T*
(appeal to economic harmony often is the cry of "peace, peace, where) Tj T*
(there is no peace." The highest social result may be attained now by) Tj T*
(limiting, again by directing, in other cases possibly by fostering,) Tj T*
(competition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Forces opposing competition]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _The main rivals of competition are custom, religion, morality,) Tj T*
(combination, and state action._ The first three of these were the) Tj T*
(strongest forces in the past and they are still operating; but) Tj T*
(combination and state action are more characteristic of the present. The) Tj T*
(influence of custom, of morality, and of religion on value, has been) Tj T*
(touched upon at several points in our study; that of combination has) Tj T*
(been recently and more fully discussed. But state action, one of the) Tj T*
(most important of all the limitations, has been reserved for the) Tj T*
(concluding portion of our work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: The state's part in directing competition]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. _It is a function of the state to determine in part the ways in which) Tj T*
(men shall exert their powers._ This is not the sole function of the) Tj T*
(state, nor is its influence toward this end exclusive. The state puts) Tj T*
(limits to the physical rivalry of men. In the distant past no doubt) Tj T*
(physical rivalry between men was an agent of progress. The strong drove) Tj T*
(out the weak; physical contest developed more vigorous limbs, keener) Tj T*
(senses, and higher sagacity. To-day it is one of the principal functions) Tj T*
(of the state to suppress the physical contest between men. The citizen) Tj T*
(is surrounded with a network of rules and regulations of which he is) Tj T*
(hardly conscious. Most men easily avoid coming into contact with the) Tj T*
(police and feel no irksomeness in the control of the civil courts. The) Tj T*
(state regulates economic interests in many other ways; it controls the) Tj T*
(building of streets; it inspects the material and construction of) Tj T*
