() Tj T*
(3. _Coinage is the act of shaping and marking a piece of metal to be) Tj T*
(used as money so as to indicate its weight and fineness._ The precious) Tj T*
(metals can and do circulate as money without coinage. Any other mark) Tj T*
(equally plain and equally recognizable serves for many purposes just as) Tj T*
(well as the government stamp on the standard metal. The use of metals in) Tj T*
(antiquity was without coinage, by weight and test of fineness. In) Tj T*
(backward countries to-day most payments are made by weight.) Tj T*
(International payments are made by means of gold ingots that bear the) Tj T*
(mark of some well-known banking-house, and for that purpose gold bullion) Tj T*
(is money without the coiner's stamp. But for most uses government) Tj T*
(coinage has marked advantages. It is far more convenient for the average) Tj T*
(citizen to handle coins uniform in size and design than the diverse) Tj T*
(coins that would be put out by private enterprisers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Technical features of coinage]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An established rate of fineness insuring uniform quality is a great) Tj T*
(convenience. In the United States all gold and silver coins are nine) Tj T*
(tenths fine; in Great Britain, eleven twelfths. The established weight) Tj T*
(of the gold dollar in the United States is twenty-three and twenty-two) Tj T*
(hundredths grains of fine gold or twenty-five and eight tenths grains of) Tj T*
(standard gold. The limit of tolerance is the variation either above or) Tj T*
(below the standard weight or fineness that a coin is allowed to have) Tj T*
(when it leaves the mint. The par of exchange between standard coins of) Tj T*
(different countries is the expression of the ratio of fine gold in them.) Tj T*
(Thus the par of exchange between the American dollar and the English) Tj T*
(sovereign \(the "pound"\) is four and eighty-six and two third hundredths,) Tj T*
(that is, four and eighty-six and two third hundredths dollars contain) Tj T*
(the same amount of gold as an English gold sovereign. The embossed) Tj T*
(design, milled or lettered edges, and other similar devices are merely) Tj T*
(to make the coins easily recognizable and difficult to counterfeit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Seigniorage defined]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
