(coinage, or it is the charge made for coinage._ Coinage as a function of) Tj T*
(great importance politically as well as economically was early exercised) Tj T*
(by governments or rulers. The prince, king, or emperor stamped his own) Tj T*
(device or portrait upon the coin; hence the term seigniorage from) Tj T*
(seignior \(meaning lord or ruler\). The right to issue money came to be) Tj T*
(one of the most essential prerogatives of sovereignty. Coinage is rarely) Tj T*
(without charge, and often has been a source of revenue to the ruler. In) Tj T*
(the Middle Ages this right was frequently exercised by princes for their) Tj T*
(selfish advantage to the injury and unsettling of trade.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
