(the same ratio as before to the total value of money. Taking an extreme) Tj T*
(case: if twice as many dollars get into circulation in a community,) Tj T*
(either some few men must have several times as many dollars as before,) Tj T*
(while others have the same; or every man will have his due proportion,) Tj T*
(just twice as much as before. The latter, "other things being equal,") Tj T*
(must be the logical result after equilibrium has been restored. Is any) Tj T*
