([Sidenote: Definition of the standard]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _The standard of deferred payments is the thing of value in which, by) Tj T*
(the law or by contract, the amount of a debt is expressed._ A credit) Tj T*
(transaction is a lengthened exchange; one party fulfils his part of the) Tj T*
(contract, the other party promises to give an equivalent at a later) Tj T*
(date. The equivalent may be in any kind of goods; for example, in barter) Tj T*
(one may part with a horse on the promise of a cow to be received later;) Tj T*
(or a small horse on the promise of a large one; or a flock of sheep on) Tj T*
(the promise of its return at the end of the year with a part of the) Tj T*
(increase of the flock. A simple standard in which to express the debt is) Tj T*
(the thing borrowed, as horse, sheep, wheat, house, etc. This involves) Tj T*
(the use of the renting contract. Again, the thing to which the value of) Tj T*
(debts is referred may be a thing quite different from the goods) Tj T*
(borrowed, and with the growth of the money economy and the use of the) Tj T*
(interest contract, money comes more and more to be used as the standard.) Tj T*
(The parties express the debt in terms of the standard unit established) Tj T*
(by law.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Increasing use of the interest contract]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _The importance of the standard of deferred payments increases with) Tj T*
(the use of money and with the amount of outstanding debts._ Until the) Tj T*
(use of money develops, the use of credit is difficult and limited; it) Tj T*
(becomes easy when the value of all things is expressed in terms of a) Tj T*
(common circulating medium. If all business were done for cash there) Tj T*
(would be no great interests affected when a change in the value of) Tj T*
(money occurred. Every dollar would change in value in the hands of the) Tj T*
(holder, but there the effect would cease. But the volume of outstanding) Tj T*
(debts expressed in terms of money now exceeds many fold the total value) Tj T*
(of the circulating medium. The value of all these debts changes in the) Tj T*
(same proportion as does that of the standard unit of money; when this is) Tj T*
(cheapened either by law or as a result of increasing supplies, a) Tj T*
(creditor to whom a thousand dollars are due loses the same as if he had) Tj T*
