(4. _Various ideals for a standard of deferred payments have been) Tj T*
(suggested--as return of equal enjoyment, of equal sacrifice, social) Tj T*
(expediency; and various standards--as labor, commodities, and the) Tj T*
(tabular standard._ The ideal standard of deferred payments is one that) Tj T*
(will insure justice between borrower and lender. Different views have) Tj T*
(been taken as to what constitutes justice in this matter. The suggestion) Tj T*
(is attractive that the sum when returned should represent the same) Tj T*
(amount of enjoyment as it did when it was borrowed. Such a standard is) Tj T*
(impossible of realization in any general way, for men's circumstances) Tj T*
(are constantly changing. To insure even to the average man the same) Tj T*
(amount of enjoyment is only roughly possible. The same goods do not) Tj T*
(afford the same enjoyment when conditions have changed. Another) Tj T*
(suggestion is that the goods returned should represent the same) Tj T*
(sacrifice as those loaned. Here again the difficulty is in the lack of) Tj T*
(an objective standard. Whose sacrifice? That of the lender, who may be) Tj T*
(rich, or that of the borrower, who may be poor? Some have supposed the) Tj T*
(conditions of equal sacrifice were met by the labor standard, according) Tj T*
(to which the sum returned should purchase the same number of days of) Tj T*
(labor as when borrowed. But what kind of labor is to be taken, that of) Tj T*
(the lender or that of the borrower, or that of some one else? Labor is) Tj T*
(of many different qualities, which can be exactly compared only through) Tj T*
(their objective value in terms of some one good. The ideal of equal) Tj T*
(enjoyment has been supposed to be realized by the tabular standard,) Tj T*
(which consists of a number of leading commodities in fixed proportions.) Tj T*
(The money returned is to be enough to purchase the same goods at the) Tj T*
(expiration as at the making of the loan, and thus may be a larger or) Tj T*
(smaller sum than was borrowed. While this does not, as is sometimes) Tj T*
(claimed, insure equality of enjoyment, it averages the fluctuations of) Tj T*
(many goods, and thus prevents great extremes. This standard has been) Tj T*
(favored by notable monetary authorities, but the difficulties of its) Tj T*
(practical application are prohibitive.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It must be recognized that any possible concrete standard of deferred) Tj T*
(payments will sometimes work hardship to individuals. The best average) Tj T*
(results for justice and social welfare will be secured by measuring) Tj T*
(debts in goods that change least often, least rapidly, and in the least) Tj T*
(unpredictable manner. Gold thus far has proved itself worthy to serve as) Tj T*
(the standard.) Tj T*
