(against foreign foes, and they need more often, relatively, defense) Tj T*
(against the aggressions of some of their own countrymen. The) Tj T*
(preservation of domestic order requires police, courts of justice, and) Tj T*
(other agencies. The ideal of the anarchist to do without government is) Tj T*
(nowhere realized. Everywhere there must be government to preserve peace) Tj T*
(and to protect property. Unfortunately, this need grows with the growing) Tj T*
(density of population. Crime increases when men swarm in great cities.) Tj T*
(To maintain and operate the social machinery requires ever-increasing) Tj T*
(resources. The courts which settle disputes between men, and which) Tj T*
(interpret their contracts, are agencies of peace, displacing physical) Tj T*
(contests. Many other public expenses tend to enlarge, as those for) Tj T*
(legislative bodies, public buildings, statistical inquiries, the) Tj T*
(printing of public documents. Government on these accounts has become in) Tj T*
(modern times an increasingly costly institution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Developing public wants; social and industrial welfare]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _The promotion of the social and industrial welfare of society has) Tj T*
(come to be an important purpose of taxation._ Some functions of) Tj T*
(government, less essential than the primary ones just mentioned, seem) Tj T*
(naturally to grow out of them. In a democratic society, popular) Tj T*
(education is one of the necessary conditions of good government, as it) Tj T*
(appears that domestic order is not possible in a democratic state) Tj T*
(without intelligent citizens. Step by step the functions of government) Tj T*
(are widened. Some industrial functions are performed by the government) Tj T*
(in connection with the primary needs. Lighthouses are necessary to guide) Tj T*
(the navy, but they also serve to guide the merchant marine and to aid) Tj T*
(industry. The post was established as an agent of political and military) Tj T*
(government to connect the ruler with the outposts \(a fact the name post) Tj T*
(indicates\), but the postal service has grown in every country to be a) Tj T*
(great industrial and social agency. The consular service, beginning in) Tj T*
(the political need of keeping official representatives in foreign lands,) Tj T*
(has grown to be a great economic agency. Consuls are commercial) Tj T*
(travelers, advancing the trade-interests of their countries in all) Tj T*
(quarters of the globe. These social and industrial functions have been) Tj T*
(increasing of late. As the national and local governments engage more in) Tj T*
(industry, they usually make larger demands in the shape of taxation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: The sphere of the state expands]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is along the border-line between the primary and the secondary) Tj T*
(purposes of taxation that the contest goes on regarding the proper) Tj T*
(functions of government. If they are to stop short of the extreme of) Tj T*
(socialism, where shall the line be drawn? The movement has been of late) Tj T*
(toward greater government activity; more of the wants of men are thus) Tj T*
(supplied through the agency of the state. That year by year a greater) Tj T*
(sum is taken by taxation and spent for the citizen is a fact that may be) Tj T*
(recognized without debate here. The toll-road becomes a public road, the) Tj T*
(toll-bridge becomes free, more is supplied by taxation for schools, for) Tj T*
(advanced research, and for technical training. In our country great) Tj T*
(wealth was given by the Morrill Act to scientific and technical schools.) Tj T*
