([Sidenote: On business]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. _Taxes usually are a portion taken from the income arising from labor) Tj T*
(or from wealth._ In rare cases more than the net income of wealth may be) Tj T*
(taken, but the aim of taxation in general is to take only a portion of) Tj T*
(the income for public uses. As economic income has many sources, it may) Tj T*
(be intercepted at many different points, and taxation may take various) Tj T*
(forms. First, private income may be appropriated by a tax on income.) Tj T*
(This is the simplest in thought, but the administrative difficulties of) Tj T*
(the income-tax are great in practice. It is not easy to determine the) Tj T*
(money value of the various sources of enjoyment that come into a man's) Tj T*
(possession in the course of a year, including, as the ideal requires,) Tj T*
(the immaterial gratifications along with the material. A second form is) Tj T*
(a tax on property in proportion to value. Since the value of material) Tj T*
(wealth is the capitalization of the rentals at the prevailing rate of) Tj T*
(interest, the property tax, so far as it applies to material wealth,) Tj T*
(should take an approximately equal proportion of incomes. If it were) Tj T*
(accurately assessed, it would be in some respects better than a tax on) Tj T*
(actual rents, for it reaches the prospective, or speculative, rental. A) Tj T*
(third form of tax is one on consumption, or expenditure. This is but) Tj T*
(another mode of attacking income, for in the long run income is spent,) Tj T*
(not always by the individual who earned it, but by some one, and thus it) Tj T*
(is reached by a tax on expenditure. The principal consumption taxes in) Tj T*
(the United States are the tariff duties and the internal revenues of the) Tj T*
(national government. In time of war, internal revenues are extended in) Tj T*
(the United States to a multitude of articles, but usually they are) Tj T*
(limited \(with minor exceptions\) to liquor and tobacco. A fourth form of) Tj T*
(tax is one on selected agencies of industry; such are business taxes,) Tj T*
(licenses, taxes on investment in business, corporation taxes, etc. These) Tj T*
(burdens are diffused and rest eventually on some income, not always) Tj T*
(exactly ascertainable. Actual tax systems combine these forms in great) Tj T*
(variety, subtracting many minute fractions from each citizen's income in) Tj T*
(ways unsuspected by him.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: Changes of taxation and in capitalization]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _The immediate effect of a change in the form of taxation is a change) Tj T*
(in the market value of goods._ If the new tax reduces the net rent of) Tj T*
(any productive agent, it reduces likewise its value, which is but the) Tj T*
(capitalization of its net rental. If taxes are taken off of factories) Tj T*
(and put upon farm rents, factories rise and farm-land falls in value.) Tj T*
(The immediate change in value is much greater than the annual tax, for) Tj T*
(if five dollars is to be taken permanently from the annual rental of the) Tj T*
(farm, nearly one hundred dollars is taken at once from its selling) Tj T*
(value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Taxes are reckoned by enterprisers as a part of the cost of production) Tj T*
(whenever the conditions of competition and of substitution make it) Tj T*
(possible to do so. In such a case the products rise in price and most of) Tj T*
(the tax falls upon the consumers. In the Civil War an increase in the) Tj T*
(tax on whisky increased its selling price, and distillers who owned) Tj T*
(stocks on which a smaller tax had already been paid reaped profits of) Tj T*
