(cost._ When reasonably understood, this proposition does not apply to a) Tj T*
(higher charge for goods of greater bulk, as more per pound for feathers) Tj T*
(than for iron, the "dead weight" of car being much greater in one case) Tj T*
(than in the other. It does not apply where there is a difference in) Tj T*
(risk, as in carrying bricks and powder, or coal and crockery; nor where) Tj T*
(there is a difference in trouble, as in shipping live stock and wheat.) Tj T*
(Any difference that can reasonably be explained as due to a difference) Tj T*
(in cost is not discrimination; on the other hand a difference in cost) Tj T*
(without a difference in rate is discrimination. Discrimination as to) Tj T*
(goods may be by value, as low rates for heavy, cheap goods and high) Tj T*
(rates for lighter, valuable ones. Coal always goes at a low rate as) Tj T*
(compared with dry goods, and sometimes more is charged for coal to be) Tj T*
