(looking deeper, they saw sources of misery in the scantiness of man's) Tj T*
(environment, and in the sloth, ignorance, and incapacity of human) Tj T*
(nature. The pessimists--the communists, and socialists of that) Tj T*
(day--seeing the same evils, had other explanations to offer. While the) Tj T*
(economists of that day believed the conditions of poverty and misery to) Tj T*
(be inevitable, the pessimists pronounced them unendurable, and advocated) Tj T*
(a radical social change as the only hope of saving the masses from) Tj T*
(starvation. In such a variety of mutually contradictory views there must) Tj T*
(have been much error, but likewise much truth if it could be) Tj T*
(disentangled.) Tj T*
