(market; but despite the great areas since brought into the) Tj T*
(world-markets, the false idea of a century ago still persists in the) Tj T*
(text-books, and shapes economic reasoning. It is vain to say that the) Tj T*
(circumstances have been unique and that the general principle is still) Tj T*
(valid. Much of the so-called orthodox economic analysis was essentially) Tj T*
(erroneous as applied to the conditions of the past century; it is) Tj T*
(erroneous to-day and will be so for years to come, if it ever fits the) Tj T*
